2	 * Backfill (ISC-4, ISC-6, ISC-12, ISC-17).
3	 *
4	 * Pulls a tenant's full transaction history from a parameterised start date
5	 * (default two years, ISC-6) up to today, paging the PocketSmith transactions
6	 * endpoint to completion (ISC-4) and upserting each page through the Store.
7	 * Every transaction keeps its verbatim source JSON (ISC-12).
8	 *
9	 * Non-destructive (ISC-17): upserts refresh base fields only via the Store's
10	 * ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE; the overlay lives in transaction_overrides, which this
11	 * module never reads or writes. Re-running a backfill is therefore safe — base
12	 * facts are refreshed, user overrides are untouched.
13	 *
14	 * Pull-only (ISC-9): the only PocketSmith traffic is the GET pagination in the
15	 * client. No listener, webhook, or push path is involved.
16	 */
17	
